  "answer": "**Final status: passed.** All three configured stages (build, unit, component) passed on the second run, `20261021T110435Z-58620c`. It took one fix cycle.\n\n**What failed:** The first run, `20261021T110338Z-71b1ec`, built fine but failed at the unit stage. One test failed on both target frameworks: `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`. The component stage was skipped because of that. The test expected `<absent>` in the output and got `expected: <not present>`.\n\n**Root cause:** When a field is in the actual response but not in the expected body, `DeltaFormatter` printed `<not present>` instead of `<absent>`. `<absent>` is the wording in the feature spec (`.lattice/context/assert-002-field-level-failure-output.md`) and in `CHANGELOG.md`, so the code was wrong, not the test.\n\n**What changed:** One line, in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`: `TestColor.Subtle(\"<not present>\")` became `TestColor.Subtle(\"<absent>\")`. No other code uses the old wording, and no tests were changed.\n\nThe verification config only runs build, unit and component. Integration and skills checks (`make integration`, `make skills`) aren't in it, so they weren't run. Nothing has been committed.",
